    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5891" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Būtŏs</span></b> , i,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βοῦτος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the chief city of
			the</i> nomos Ptenethu <i>in Egypt</i>, <i>upon the Sebennytic mouth of the Nile; containing a
				famous temple and oracle of Latona</i> (<i>Buto</i>), <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 10, 11, §
			64</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Būtĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of Butos</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">linum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 1, 2, § 14</span></i>
			.</div>
